From 5df0bd3f62c812b82016e2ec0f0d46907493a1ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:58:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban sync: the live resync sweep bounds task_links
 to links present when the rebuild began

PR #2571 review (t_01a1d6519629121a): task_links has no creation time, so the `since` guard never covered it. A
link written after held_at_start and acked by a concurrent reconcile after the task_links snapshot was read had
no op, no tombstone and no snapshot row, and the sweep deleted and tombstoned it while the Board held it.
held_at_start now records every task_links uid (read before the outbox), and the sweep spares any link not in
that set.

The creation-time guard is now `created_at < since`: `since` is read before held_at_start, so a row written in
that same second after held_at_start was unguarded. Such a row is spared for one more rebuild instead.

Tests: an acked-mid-rebuild link survives (RED before: swept + tombstoned), a link present at start is still
swept, a same-second row is not swept (RED before). #2588's child since-guard test now pins the `<` boundary
(a comment at `since` is spared, one at `since - 1` is swept).

